{# AO · THE RIGHT-NOW STRIP — and the clearest place the seam shows.

   The host draws no tile of its own except the summary of its own attention list: every other
   tile was returned by an installed module's provider, and the index prefix says which. Install a
   module and its tiles join the row; uninstall it and they leave. Nothing here is a hard-coded
   list.

   A module with nothing to say contributes no tile — ABSENT IS NOT ZERO. When no module has
   anything to say at all, the strip says so in one line rather than drawing an empty row.
   → Uhifadhi\Service\AreaOverviewComposer::nowTiles #}
{% if tiles is empty %}
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab"><span class="idx">AO·02</span>Right now</span>
        {{ include('area/overview/_ao_by.html.twig', {slug: 'host', who: 'host · module tiles'}, with_context: false) }}
        <div class="use">Nothing is reporting into this strip. Every tile on it is contributed by a module installed in
            this area — so an empty strip means either a quiet morning or no module that measures one.</div>
    </div>
{% else %}
    <div class="grid w-flush dp-kstrip">
        {% for tile in tiles %}
            <div class="c kpi{{ tile.tone == 'hot' ? ' hot' }}{{ tile.tone == 'bad' ? ' bad' }}">
                <span class="tab">
                    <span class="idx">{{ tile.index }}</span>{{ tile.label }}
                    {%- if tile.live %}<span class="src">· <span class="ao-live"><i></i></span></span>{% endif -%}
                </span>
                <b class="disp">{{ tile.value }}{% if tile.unit %}<em>{{ tile.unit }}</em>{% endif %}</b>
                <span class="sub">
                    {{- tile.subline -}}
                    {%- if tile.alarm %}{{ tile.subline ? ' · ' }}<span class="r">{{ tile.alarm }}</span>{% endif -%}
                </span>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
